review.reviewBody:
I made the following substitutions:

1) I didn't have crescent rolls, so I just used a regular pie crust and it was fine;

2) I had lemon pepper seasoning in my pantry, so I added in 1 TBL.. of that and it really worked well in the quiche;

3) I added in 1 tsp. of nutmeg. I thought that was such a nice compliment to the spinach, mushrooms, and lemon pepper.

Next time, I'm going to switch out the whipped cream and replace it with low-fat evaporated milk to cut the calories and fat grams. Thanks for sharing such a nice recipe. This quiche is perfect for a brunch, shower or light dinner.
